{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1549664-the-point-of-weaker-immortals","id":1549664,"title":"The point of weaker immortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-31T04:17:48-07:00","id":1549664,"title":"The point of weaker immortals","content":"Whats the point of weaker immortals like the blood bathers and reborn or even any that are not a mummy?<br /> The player characters are walking disasters that can solo armies. What sort of a challenge do those antagonists pose to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T04:38:00-07:00","id":1549666,"title":"","content":"Ability to play on the same timescales as the Arisen without as intensive an upkeep mechanism as Descent checks nor as severe a handicap as Memory loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:38:04-07:00","id":1549681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1549664-the-point-of-weaker-immortals?p=1549666#post1549666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ability to play on the same timescales as the Arisen without as intensive an upkeep mechanism as Descent checks nor as severe a handicap as Memory loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, plus they are not merely antagonists. They can be allies or even touchstones, and they're valuable because of their immortality and what that means in a world where very few creatures, even supernatural, can relate to mummies' relationship with time. Even as antagonists, they can be part of a larger cult, so even if they are individually weaker than the mummy, they may be hiding a more powerful and dangerous opponent who is pulling the real strings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T15:39:34-07:00","id":1549754,"title":"","content":"Memory as a mechanic alone makes these &quot;lesser&quot; immortals important. They dont have NEAR the issue mummies or even vampires have with memory<br /> <br /> These Endless can be antagonists merely because they met the Mummy at a different point in time and remember something he DOESNT","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T04:41:15-07:00","id":1549772,"title":"","content":"Also, the Purified having their own cults dedicated to ancestor worship, training their chosen disciples to learn immortality too, working over centuries to undermine a mummy's cult when the Mummy isn't active could well present a decent challenge on their own (especially if they simply gain rank by spending XP, as appears to be the case)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T04:58:32-07:00","id":1549773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1549664-the-point-of-weaker-immortals?p=1549754#post1549754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Memory as a mechanic alone makes these &quot;lesser&quot; immortals important. They dont have NEAR the issue mummies or even vampires have with memory<br /> <br /> These Endless can be antagonists merely because they met the Mummy at a different point in time and remember something he DOESNT</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point. One could have very interesting chronicles built around an immortal who has memories that mummies and vampires alike have forgotten (or remember incorrectly). Their being more squishy than Arisen and Kindred makes them all the more valuable to preserve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T17:08:15-07:00","id":1549832,"title":"","content":"1. Lets you keep allies and enemies around between big gaps in time, so you can do flash backs or time travel stories without issue.<br /> <br /> 2. Gives the game more variety and creates more diverse stories. Immortals have their own ways of staying alive and therefore their own concerns. But as noted, they lack the power of a mummy. Which means they can also be easy plot devices when some of those unusual concerns prove too big for an immortal to handle and they need a favor from the local army leveling powerhouse. <br /> <br /> 3. Frankly World of Darkness: immortals was a good product and interaction between the subject of that book and Arisen was only natural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T14:31:34-07:00","id":1550177,"title":"","content":"More like: World of Darkness: Immortals was a good product but wasn't going to be getting a 2e update, and tying it into Mummy: the Curse gave a good reason to update them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T07:52:39-07:00","id":1551341,"title":"","content":"Is it true that the Purified are based on the immortals from Highlander?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T08:12:52-07:00","id":1551343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1549664-the-point-of-weaker-immortals?p=1551341#post1551341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it true that the Purified are based on the immortals from Highlander?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly not; the Harvesters from WoD: Immortals are notionally closer to the &quot;immortals who kill other immortals for magical gain&quot; premise, but they're people attuned to a particularly deadly magical object that converts centuries of a supernatural creature's lived life into years of extra life. The Purified are people who have undergone a ritual procedure that essentially converts their soul into a spirit and gives them attendant supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T11:29:09-07:00","id":1551367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1549664-the-point-of-weaker-immortals?p=1551343#post1551343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Almost certainly not; the Harvesters from WoD: Immortals are notionally closer to the &quot;immortals who kill other immortals for magical gain&quot; premise, but they're people attuned to a particularly deadly magical object that converts centuries of a supernatural creature's lived life into years of extra life. The Purified are people who have undergone a ritual procedure that essentially converts their soul into a spirit and gives them attendant supernatural powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically I'd say the most obvious source of inspiration is from the classic World of Darkness game Mummy the Resurrection, particularly the 'Chinese mummy' Wu Tian from that product. Since Immortals was written at a time before Mummy the Curse came out I saw it as an effort to bring over the older game into what was then called the New World of Darkness (then again I see elements of Resurrection in stuff like the Osiris Lineage of Prometheans or the whole deal with death spirit stuff from Geist).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}